    exampleHands: [
      'Setup example: 13 card(s) per player.',
      'Rule example: Be first to shed all cards (Daifugō = 1st place). Avoid being last (Daihinmin = last place).',
      'Turn-flow example: The player holding 3♦ (or 3♠ in some variants) leads first. On each turn, a player may:\n- Play a combination STRICTLY HIGHER than the previous combination of the SAME TYPE (single, pair, triple, sequence of 3+).\n- Or pass.\nThe played combination must match the current type (if singles are out, you must play singles). The round continues until all but one player passes; then the last player to play leads a new combination.',
      'Scoring example: Ranking system (1st to last) determines next round exchanges. First to shed all cards = Daifugō (1st place)..',
